## Customize flags given to the VM: https://www.erlang.org/doc/man/erl.html
## -mode/-name/-sname/-setcookie are configured via env vars — do not set them here.
##
## Tuned for a 512 MB / ~0.5 vCPU Render container. Before this file existed the
## release ran with stock settings, which is what made the box OOM: see the
## scheduler note below.

## ---- Schedulers -------------------------------------------------------------
## The BEAM sizes its scheduler count from the *host* core count, not the cgroup
## CPU quota. On a shared Render host that means 8+ normal schedulers plus 8+
## dirty ones, each carrying its own set of allocator arenas — 100+ MB of pure
## overhead before a single request is served. Pin them to the CPU we actually
## have.
+S 2:2
+SDcpu 2:2
+SDio 4

## Busy-wait keeps schedulers spinning between jobs. That holds allocator
## carriers hot and burns a CPU quota we do not have.
+sbwt none
+sbwtdcpu none
+sbwtdio none

## ---- Allocators -------------------------------------------------------------
## Address-order best-fit fragments far less than the default strategy for the
## mixed allocation sizes a Phoenix request produces.
+MBas aobf
+MHas aobf
+MEas aobf

## Cap the largest multiblock carrier (default 10 MB) so memory freed after a
## traffic spike is returned to the OS instead of being held in the carrier.
## Values are in KB.
+MBlmbcs 5120
+MHlmbcs 5120
+MElmbcs 5120

## ---- Per-process heap ceiling ------------------------------------------------
## 4M words ~= 32 MB per process on 64-bit. An unbounded Repo.all that would
## otherwise OOM-kill the whole container instead kills ONE request process and
## logs a stacktrace naming the query.
##
## Note this bounds the *process* heap, so it catches struct accumulation
## (the unpaginated index pages) but NOT large binaries, which live on the
## shared binary heap — that is what the chunked CSV exports are for.
+hmax 4000000
+hmaxel true
+hmaxk true
